  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "The graph, \\(G,\\) of \\(y=\\log_{10}x\\) is rotated \\(90^\\circ\\) counter-clockwise about the origin to obtain a new graph \\(G'.\\) Which of the following is an equation for \\(G'?\\)",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(y=\\log_{10}\\left(\\frac{x+90}{9}\\right)\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(y=\\log_x10\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(y=\\frac1{x+1}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(y=10^{-x}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(y=10^x\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "d",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1991-p24.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "A point \\((u,\\log_{10}u)\\) rotates to \\[ (x,y)=(-\\log_{10}u,u). \\] Hence \\(x=-\\log_{10}y,\\) so \\(\\log_{10}y=-x\\) and \\(y=10^{-x}.\\)\n\nThus the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "A \\(90^\\circ\\) counter-clockwise rotation sends \\((x,y)\\) to \\((-y,x)\\)",
        "Rename the rotated coordinates and solve the logarithmic relation for the new \\(y\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
